Group B: Long Questions

5. Explain the ”F-Pattern” of scanning and how it influences the placement of content on a web page.
ans: F pattern describes how users commonly scan web pages , especially text-heavy pages rather than reading every word. Eye tracking studies(notably by Nielsen Norman Group ) show that users eyes move in a pattern that riughly looks like the letter "F".
How F-pattern works
 Users typically scan a page in three main steps:
1. Top Horizontal Scan
•Users read across the top part of the page.
•This is where attention is highest.
•Example:Page title, main navigation , headline.

2. Second Horizontal Scan
•Users move down slightly and scan across again.
•This line is usually shorter the the first.
•Rxample:Subheading or the first line of the content.

3. Vertical scan(Left side)
•Users then scan down from the left side of the page.
•The look for keywords , bullet points or links.

Influnce on Content Placement:
1. Important information at the Top
•places headlines , key messages and navigation menus at the top.
•Users see these first before deciding whether to continue.

2. key Contents on the left 
•Important links , menus and Keywords should be left aligned.
•Users spend more time scanning the left side than the right.

3. Less Focus on Right side
•Contents placed on the far right gets less attention from the user.
•Avoid placing critical information on the right side.


