7. Explain the ”60-30-10 Rule” regarding color balance on a website.
ans: The 60-30-10 rule is a simple and effective guidelines used in web and UI design to create a balanced , visually pleasing color scheme. It explaons how to proportionally use colors on a websites so that it looks organixed and easy to understand.

What The 60-30-10 Rule means:
The rule divides colors into three parts:
1. 60% - Primary Color:
•This is the main background color of the website.
•Sets the overall mood and the theme.
•Usually a neutral or soft color.

Examples:White Light gray , soft Blue.
Used for:
•Page background.
•Large content areas.

2. 30% - Secondary Color:
•Supports and contrasts the primary color.
•Adds visual interest without overwhelming the design.
Examples:Dark blue , gray , muted green

Used for;
•Headers
•navigation bars
•Sidebars

3.10% - Accent color:
•A bold , eye catching color.
•Used sparingly to drae attention to important elements.
Examples:Red , Orange

Used for:
•call-to -Action button 
•Links and icons

Example of 60-30-10 Rule on a website
•60% White : Background
•30% Blue : Navigation bar , headings
•10% Red : "sign up" button

