8. A website loads very slowly, causing users to abandon it. Upon inspection, you find the developer used high-resolution raw images directly from a camera. Explain the importance of Image Optimization and file formats (JPEG vs PNG) to solve this.
ans: In this scenario , the developer used high - resolution raw images directly forma camera , which are usually very large in file size (often several MBs per image). This can dramatically slow down page loading.

Optimizing images solves this problem by reduucing file size wothout significantly reducing visual quality.
Importance of Image Optimization:
1. Faster loading Speed 
•Smaller images load faster , improving user experience.
•Faster pages improves SEO ranking.

2. Better Performance Across Devices
•optimized images work well on moblie devices with limited bandwodth.
•Reduces data usage for users.

3. Improved Accessibility
•Faster loading pages are more acsessible to users with slow internet.

4. Reduced server load
•Smaller files takes less storage and bandwidth , sacing hosting costs.

Choosing the right file format
1. JPEG(Joint Photographic Experts Group)
Best for: Photographs , images with gradients , real life pictures.
Pros:
•Compressed(smaller file sizes).
•Good quality at reasonable compression.

Cons:
•Uses lossy compression(some wuality is lost).
•Not ideal for images with sharp edges or text.

Usecase:Product photos, banners, background

2.PNG(Portable Network Graphics)
Best for:Images with transoarency , icons , logos , diagrams.
Pros:
•Losless compression(no quality loss)
•Supports transparent background

Cons:
•larger file size than JPEG

Use Case:Logos ,Ui elementd , icons

Conclusion:By resizing images and using JPEg and PNG obly when transparency is needed , the website performance can br greatly improved.


